      "side": 1,
      "message": "Design concern: this fail-open behavior means a misspelled/disabled switch_vendor tag silently skips the port while move/validate/release all report success — the host keeps its old VLAN config in a production move. A case-sensitive typo like \"Arista\" or \"arista \" has the same effect. Consider validating switch_vendor against enabled plugin names at interface create/update time, or at minimum warn loudly in the dispatcher when a host\u0027s interfaces are claimed by no plugin.",
      "revId": "5ec35ddcb58a94477c496dce5f20d1f94223a05f",
      "serverId": "d5d70762-12d0-45a1-890d-524b12d3f735"
    },
