      "writtenOn": "2026-10-16T19:25:26Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Agreed, and the consequence was worse than the text said: because `configure()` returned `True` for a host it never touched, `--move-hosts` wrote `switch_config_applied: True` (cli.py:2082) and `--validate-env` then skipped that host for good (environment.py:227), so no fallback could see the skipped port.\n\nFixed in the plugins rather than at the API: `SwitchPlugin` now exposes `unclaimed_interfaces()` and `log_unclaimed()` (plugins/interfaces/switch.py:27,34), and `configure()`, `modify()` and `verify()` fail closed with a loud error naming the interfaces and the offending `switch_vendor` values when no enabled switch plugin claims them. The move is then recorded as failed and `switch_config_applied` stays false, so validation keeps reporting the host until the tag is fixed.\n\nNot added: validation at interface create/update. The API server\u0027s plugin configuration is not necessarily the mover\u0027s, and a hard reject also blocks the legitimate \"plugin disabled while we work on it\" case. The escape hatches are unchanged: fix the tag or enable the plugin (now spelled out at docs/switch-host-setup.md:162), or use `omit_network_move` (conf/quads.yml) or set `switch_config_applied` by hand (README) as before.\n\nTests: a typo\u0027d vendor fails closed in both plugins, and a correctly tagged mixed-vendor host still programs exactly the same ports as before.",
      "parentUuid": "03958f44_e7e55333",
      "revId": "5ec35ddcb58a94477c496dce5f20d1f94223a05f",
      "serverId": "d5d70762-12d0-45a1-890d-524b12d3f735"
    },
