      "writtenOn": "2026-10-16T18:18:33Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "modify() returns True here even when `success` was False above (line 189-192): a failed set_port()/set_port_qinq() is only logged, then this return True makes the dispatcher treat the whole operation as successful. test_modify_set_port_failure asserts `result is True` for exactly this case. configure() and verify() fail closed — modify() should propagate the failure too (return False / all_ok flag), otherwise `--mod-interface --change` reports success while the port was never touched.",
      "revId": "5ec35ddcb58a94477c496dce5f20d1f94223a05f",
      "serverId": "d5d70762-12d0-45a1-890d-524b12d3f735"
