      "writtenOn": "2026-10-16T19:25:26Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Confirmed and fixed in PS9. `modify()` now carries an `all_ok` flag: a failed `set_port()`/`set_port_qinq()` logs the error, sets `all_ok \u003d False` and `modify()` returns it (arista.py:205,210), so the dispatcher no longer counts the operation as successful. `test_modify_set_port_failure` now asserts `is False`.\n\nRelated: the rejection path was dead before, because the driver compared a bytes `child.before` against a str `\"%\"`, so every command raised `TypeError` and only a 120s pexpect timeout could ever return `False` (see the external/arista.py thread). Both had to be fixed together.\n\nOne thing to know: the CLI does not consume the dispatcher result today (`action_mod_switch_conf` discards it), so the operator-visible symptom was the plugin ERROR line rather than an exit code. I left that alone; happy to make `--mod-switch-conf` exit non-zero if you want it.",
      "parentUuid": "1559219e_0ba06c05",
      "revId": "5ec35ddcb58a94477c496dce5f20d1f94223a05f",
      "serverId": "d5d70762-12d0-45a1-890d-524b12d3f735"
