      "writtenOn": "2026-10-16T18:18:33Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "verify() dead code: `_cloud` (fetched at line 210 via get_cloud(cloud)) is never assigned to `_cloud_obj`, so `_cloud_obj` is always first_host.cloud and the `if _cloud_obj !\u003d first_host.cloud:` warning at line 230 can never fire. When both host and cloud are passed (e.g. CLI `--verify-switch-conf --host X --cloud Y`), the cloud argument is silently ignored and verification runs against the host\u0027s own cloud. Fix: `_cloud_obj \u003d _cloud` when cloud is given. (Same pattern exists in juniper.py — worth fixing both.)",
      "revId": "5ec35ddcb58a94477c496dce5f20d1f94223a05f",
      "serverId": "d5d70762-12d0-45a1-890d-524b12d3f735"
