      "writtenOn": "2026-10-16T19:25:26Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Confirmed in both plugins: `_cloud` was fetched and dropped, so the warning could never fire and `--cloud` was ignored whenever `--host` was also given.\n\nI did not apply `_cloud_obj \u003d _cloud`, because that comparison is identity based: `Cloud` and `Host` define no `__eq__`, and `filter_hosts` builds fresh objects per response, so a `Cloud` from `get_cloud()` never equals `first_host.cloud` even for the same cloud. Assigning it would fire the warning on every `--verify-switch-conf --cloud cloud0X` run with self-contradictory text, and `_assignment` would come from the other cloud, which under `--change` reprograms ports against a plan that does not apply to the host.\n\nInstead (arista.py:240-247 and the same block in juniper.py): the comparison is on cloud names, the warning fires only when they really differ, its text says which cloud is used, and `_assignment` still comes from the host\u0027s own cloud, as it effectively always did.",
